WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.090
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.360 --> 01:34.900
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.270 --> 01:37.820
[Episode 58]

4
01:38.430 --> 01:41.920
This is not our final destination.

5
01:38.560 --> 01:41.170
[Ganzi, Sichuan]

6
01:42.120 --> 01:43.789
We must continue north

7
01:43.789 --> 01:45.509
to join forces with the 1st Front Army

8
01:45.509 --> 01:49.200
and march together to the front lines of the war against Japan.

9
01:49.350 --> 01:50.759
Yes!

10
02:02.000 --> 02:04.870
Now, let's welcome Comrade Ren Bishi to say a few words.

11
02:04.830 --> 02:06.010
Great!

12
02:14.240 --> 02:15.030
First,

13
02:14.850 --> 02:16.710
[Ren Bishi, Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee,]

14
02:15.310 --> 02:19.079
I'd like to pay my respects to our comrades in the 4th Front Army.

15
02:16.710 --> 02:18.579
[Political Commissar of the 2nd Red Army Corps]

16
02:19.280 --> 02:20.840
Hear, hear!

17
02:25.190 --> 02:26.310
On our way here,

18
02:26.870 --> 02:29.000
I heard from Commander-in-Chief Zhu and Comrade Liu Bocheng

19
02:29.000 --> 02:31.400
about the situation in the Shaanxi-Gansu Base Area.

20
02:31.400 --> 02:34.000
Since the 1st Front Army arrived in northern Shaanxi,

21
02:34.000 --> 02:36.800
they have won a victory in the Eastern Expedition.

22
02:37.030 --> 02:41.120
The Shaanxi-Gansu Base Area has now grown stronger and expanded,

23
02:41.280 --> 02:43.400
and the 1st Front Army has grown stronger as well.

24
02:43.400 --> 02:45.960
What's more, they are now on their Westward Expedition

25
02:45.960 --> 02:47.620
to support our advance north.

26
02:47.710 --> 02:49.430
Our only way forward

27
02:49.470 --> 02:52.000
is to answer the Party Central Committee's call

28
02:52.000 --> 02:54.710
to form an Anti-Japanese National United Front,

29
02:54.710 --> 02:56.870
and head north to join the Central Committee!

30
02:56.870 --> 02:58.560
Great!

31
03:06.840 --> 03:07.770
Comrade He Long,

32
03:08.680 --> 03:09.430
would you like to say a few words?

33
03:09.430 --> 03:10.680
Then I'll say a few words?

34
03:10.680 --> 03:11.740
Okay, let me say a few words.

35
03:11.740 --> 03:12.700
Great!

36
03:17.430 --> 03:19.000
I'll say a few words.

37
03:19.800 --> 03:20.630
First of all,

38
03:20.640 --> 03:23.840
[He Long, Commander of the 2nd Red Army Corps]

39
03:20.960 --> 03:24.310
I'd like to pay my respects to our comrades in the 4th Front Army.

40
03:24.310 --> 03:27.870
Hear, hear!

41
03:31.079 --> 03:32.240
First,

42
03:32.310 --> 03:35.470
I firmly support Commander-in-Chief Zhu's speech.

43
03:35.680 --> 03:37.079
Second, I'd like to offer

44
03:37.630 --> 03:40.000
a few minor suggestions

45
03:40.120 --> 03:42.030
to Comrade Zhang Guotao.

46
03:44.030 --> 03:45.090
What suggestions?

47
03:46.630 --> 03:47.590
Comrade Guotao,

48
03:47.960 --> 03:49.000
comrades,

49
03:49.280 --> 03:50.590
look up there.

50
03:51.240 --> 03:52.800
The banner reads,

51
03:52.800 --> 03:55.400
"Welcome Rally for the 2nd and 6th Army Corps."

52
03:55.470 --> 03:57.329
I don't think that's quite right.

53
03:57.470 --> 03:59.000
Why not?

54
03:59.400 --> 04:02.400
We of the 2nd and 6th Army Corps aren't guests here.

55
04:02.430 --> 04:05.190
We've come to join the comrades of the 4th Front Army,

56
04:05.190 --> 04:07.120
reunite in victory,

57
04:07.150 --> 04:08.610
and march north together.

58
04:08.870 --> 04:11.360
So I don't think this should be called

59
04:11.360 --> 04:13.310
the "Welcome Rally for the 2nd and 6th Army Corps."

60
04:13.310 --> 04:16.430
It should be called the "Triumphant Junction Rally."

61
04:16.950 --> 04:18.560
Don't you agree?

62
04:18.560 --> 04:19.720
Yes!

63
04:20.000 --> 04:22.360
Good, good!

64
04:32.150 --> 04:33.240
Comrade Guotao,

65
04:33.310 --> 04:34.770
don't you think I'm right?

66
04:35.120 --> 04:35.920
Yes.

67
04:37.040 --> 04:38.840
I didn't give it enough thought.

68
04:39.070 --> 04:42.330
It should indeed be called the Triumphant Junction Rally.

69
04:42.430 --> 04:43.720
Great!

70
04:43.920 --> 04:45.050
That's more like it.

71
04:46.190 --> 04:47.430
Comrades,

72
04:48.600 --> 04:50.750
Commander-in-Chief Zhu and Comrade Bishi

73
04:50.750 --> 04:52.159
have already spoken about

74
04:52.159 --> 04:53.390
the triumphant junction of our two armies,

75
04:53.390 --> 04:54.990
so I won't go over that again.

76
04:55.070 --> 04:58.190
I'd like to tell you a short story.

77
04:58.390 --> 04:59.870
Would you like to hear it?

78
05:00.070 --> 05:00.920
Yes!

79
05:00.940 --> 05:01.740
All right.

80
05:02.750 --> 05:06.160
Our 2nd and 6th Army Corps marched north from Pan County.

81
05:06.390 --> 05:08.800
The journey was extremely grueling,

82
05:09.070 --> 05:10.930
with one hardship after another.

83
05:11.000 --> 05:13.920
At the time, our 2nd Army Corps on the left flank

84
05:13.950 --> 05:15.630
was surrounded by enemy forces

85
05:15.630 --> 05:17.760
in Baan (present-day Batang County).

86
05:17.830 --> 05:19.430
We were in unfamiliar territory,

87
05:19.430 --> 05:21.360
and our troops were exhausted.

88
05:22.190 --> 05:24.190
We had no choice but to take a detour.

89
05:24.390 --> 05:26.720
One of our advance detachments

90
05:26.720 --> 05:27.750
lost its way

91
05:28.000 --> 05:29.950
and couldn't figure out which direction to go.

92
05:29.950 --> 05:31.830
So they kept heading south.

93
05:32.110 --> 05:34.190
By the time they realized their mistake,

94
05:34.190 --> 05:35.800
they had already crossed the Dulong River

95
05:35.800 --> 05:37.270
and ended up in Burma.

96
05:37.270 --> 05:40.070
They even came face-to-face with British troops.

97
05:44.950 --> 05:46.870
And what happened next, sir?

98
05:47.560 --> 05:49.600
Easy there, young man. Don't rush me.

99
05:49.600 --> 05:52.800
Well, this detachment

100
05:53.070 --> 05:54.870
asked the locals

101
05:54.870 --> 05:57.630
and got clear directions,

102
05:57.950 --> 06:01.190
then immediately turned around and went after the main force.

103
06:01.190 --> 06:03.920
They finally caught up with the main force

104
06:04.070 --> 06:06.630
in Baiyu County, in the Xikang region.

105
06:07.310 --> 06:10.390
The cadres of that detachment

106
06:10.630 --> 06:11.630
later came to me.

107
06:11.870 --> 06:13.430
They said they wanted to make a self-criticism

108
06:13.430 --> 06:15.480
and asked to be disciplined.

109
06:16.070 --> 06:17.560
But I told them,

110
06:17.830 --> 06:19.600
"You simply lost your way

111
06:19.920 --> 06:21.920
and couldn't figure out where to go.

112
06:22.270 --> 06:24.160
As long as you turned around immediately,

113
06:24.160 --> 06:25.270
got back

114
06:25.390 --> 06:26.600
on the right track,

115
06:26.830 --> 06:27.830
and caught up with the main force,

116
06:27.830 --> 06:29.360
you did a fine job.

117
06:29.480 --> 06:31.310
In fact, I'd commend you for it!"

118
06:31.390 --> 06:32.870
Don't you agree?

119
06:32.920 --> 06:33.870
Yes!

120
06:34.270 --> 06:35.680
Great!

121
06:35.680 --> 06:37.010
That's all I have to say.

122
06:38.310 --> 06:39.120
Great!

123
06:41.950 --> 06:45.040
Great!

124
06:45.040 --> 06:48.310
Now, let's hear from Comrade Zhang Guotao.

125
06:48.360 --> 06:50.750
Yeah!

126
06:58.159 --> 06:59.270
Watch what you say.

127
06:59.270 --> 07:00.390
Speak only of unity.

128
07:00.390 --> 07:01.520
Don't sow division.

129
07:03.510 --> 07:06.120
Or I'll shoot you in the back.

130
07:13.000 --> 07:14.920
Very well said.

131
07:19.600 --> 07:20.390
Comrades,

132
07:22.390 --> 07:25.600
unity is very important.

133
07:25.920 --> 07:27.560
Great!

134
07:36.720 --> 07:38.120
Zhang Guotao

135
07:38.190 --> 07:39.630
talks about unity,

136
07:39.950 --> 07:41.680
but behind our backs, he's always up to something.

137
07:41.680 --> 07:43.190
One minute he's handing out leaflets,

138
07:43.190 --> 07:44.040
the next he's

139
07:44.240 --> 07:46.310
approaching cadres of our 2nd and 6th Army Corps

140
07:46.310 --> 07:47.370
for private talks.

141
07:47.560 --> 07:49.960
He's constantly trying to win people over.

142
07:50.630 --> 07:53.510
He pulled plenty of these tricks

143
07:53.870 --> 07:55.070
when the 1st and 4th Front Armies

144
07:55.070 --> 07:56.240
joined forces.

145
07:57.270 --> 07:58.190
Commander-in-Chief,

146
07:58.190 --> 07:59.390
you can rest assured.

147
07:59.600 --> 08:01.950
Comrade Bishi has already given the order.

148
08:01.950 --> 08:04.360
We'll only let Zhang Guotao's men

149
08:04.600 --> 08:06.950
share their experience crossing the grasslands with us.

150
08:06.950 --> 08:08.510
As for the booklets they brought,

151
08:08.510 --> 08:09.560
titled What Every Cadre Should Know,

152
08:09.560 --> 08:10.830
we've put them all in the Political Department.

153
08:10.830 --> 08:12.510
Not a single copy will be distributed.

154
08:12.510 --> 08:13.630
There's one more thing.

155
08:13.630 --> 08:16.430
I'm going to hold a small meeting with the cadres

156
08:16.430 --> 08:17.680
of the 2nd and 6th Army Corps

157
08:17.680 --> 08:18.600
to make one thing clear.

158
08:18.600 --> 08:20.240
The Central Committee is in northern Shaanxi,

159
08:20.240 --> 08:21.630
and we must all follow its leadership.

160
08:21.630 --> 08:22.430
Anyone who refuses

161
08:22.430 --> 08:24.160
will have me to answer to first.

162
08:25.040 --> 08:26.640
You've done the right thing.

163
08:26.950 --> 08:29.430
I think Zhang Guotao is quite wary of you.

164
08:30.120 --> 08:31.240
At the junction rally,

165
08:31.240 --> 08:33.549
when you threatened to shoot him in the back,

166
08:33.549 --> 08:35.610
he hardly dared say a word out of line.

167
08:35.909 --> 08:37.840
Why would I shoot him in the back?

168
08:37.840 --> 08:39.770
He's just got a guilty conscience.

169
08:45.030 --> 08:46.360
Where's Comrade Bishi?

170
08:46.750 --> 08:48.670
Comrade Bishi has gone to see Fu Zhong.

171
08:48.670 --> 08:50.320
Since Zhang Guotao has been approaching

172
08:50.320 --> 08:51.910
cadres of our 2nd and 6th Army Corps for talks,

173
08:51.910 --> 08:54.150
we'll send people to talk to

174
08:54.150 --> 08:56.150
cadres of the 4th Front Army as well.

175
08:56.390 --> 08:58.510
We'll explain the Central Committee's policies to them.

176
08:58.510 --> 09:00.960
Comrade Ren Bishi is a member of the Politburo,

177
09:00.960 --> 09:02.320
just like Zhang Guotao.

178
09:02.720 --> 09:03.960
He has every right to do this.

179
09:03.960 --> 09:04.840
Let him do his part.

180
09:04.840 --> 09:06.030
We'll do ours.

181
09:09.030 --> 09:10.030
Comrade Fu Zhong,

182
09:10.550 --> 09:13.030
I've already briefed you on the conflict

183
09:13.120 --> 09:15.360
between Zhang Guotao and the Central Committee.

184
09:15.360 --> 09:16.510
What are your thoughts?

185
09:16.330 --> 09:20.280
[Fu Zhong, Deputy Director of the Political Department of the 4th Front Army]

186
09:16.960 --> 09:19.510
From what Chairman Zhang told us before,

187
09:20.480 --> 09:22.600
the Central Committee had abandoned the 4th Front Army

188
09:22.600 --> 09:24.130
and headed north on its own.

189
09:24.270 --> 09:25.440
He never explained

190
09:25.840 --> 09:27.000
the details,

191
09:27.030 --> 09:28.390
so I didn't know the full story.

192
09:28.390 --> 09:31.120
This is the first time I've heard the whole story.

193
09:31.150 --> 09:33.610
Here's what I suggest. Seeing is believing.

194
09:34.200 --> 09:36.120
You can look through the telegrams exchanged

195
09:36.120 --> 09:39.120
between the Central Committee and the 4th Front Army.

196
09:39.150 --> 09:40.550
If I'm entitled to read them as a Politburo member,

197
09:40.550 --> 09:41.360
so are you.

198
09:41.550 --> 09:43.950
Once you've seen it, the truth of the matter

199
09:44.200 --> 09:45.200
will become clear to you.

200
09:45.200 --> 09:46.030
All right.

201
09:47.240 --> 09:48.270
Comrade Fu Zhong,

202
09:48.670 --> 09:51.080
that's all for our discussion today.

203
09:51.320 --> 09:52.390
Broadly speaking,

204
09:52.630 --> 09:55.390
what we're emphasizing now is unity.

205
09:56.320 --> 09:57.870
With the war against Japanese aggression as our priority,

206
09:57.870 --> 10:00.470
all other differences can be set aside for now.

207
10:00.510 --> 10:03.670
The truth about the Central Committee will come out in time.

208
10:03.670 --> 10:04.750
Comrade Bishi,

209
10:05.670 --> 10:07.270
I have just one thing to say.

210
10:08.550 --> 10:11.600
The Party's guiding light is not here.

211
10:19.910 --> 10:21.030
Comrade Fu Zhong.

212
10:23.120 --> 10:25.050
Chief Political Commissar Zhang.

213
10:27.910 --> 10:29.240
What are you doing here?

214
10:30.030 --> 10:32.160
Comrade Bishi wanted to speak with me.

215
10:32.470 --> 10:34.530
All right. I'll leave you two to talk.

216
10:43.250 --> 10:44.410
Comrade Bishi,

217
10:45.080 --> 10:46.210
please, have a seat.

218
10:49.080 --> 10:50.320
Look at you.

219
10:50.630 --> 10:52.030
You've been traveling for so long.

220
10:52.030 --> 10:53.750
You should take some time to rest.

221
10:53.750 --> 10:55.870
The Central Committee is waiting for us to march north.

222
10:55.870 --> 10:58.120
We must bring everyone onto the same page as soon as possible.

223
10:58.120 --> 10:59.580
How can I find time to rest?

224
11:01.720 --> 11:03.000
Since we need to unite everyone's thinking,

225
11:03.000 --> 11:04.480
I suggest

226
11:04.480 --> 11:07.120
we hold a joint Party meeting

227
11:07.390 --> 11:08.720
to discuss things first

228
11:08.840 --> 11:10.200
and then reach a decision.

229
11:10.200 --> 11:11.200
What do you think?

230
11:13.270 --> 11:15.080
The Central Committee isn't here.

231
11:15.080 --> 11:16.150
If the 4th Front Army

232
11:16.150 --> 11:18.910
and the 2nd and 6th Army Corps hold a Party meeting,

233
11:18.910 --> 11:20.120
who would chair it?

234
11:20.550 --> 11:22.280
Who would present the reports?

235
11:23.480 --> 11:25.480
We're both members of the Politburo.

236
11:25.480 --> 11:26.440
If we disagree,

237
11:26.440 --> 11:28.170
whose decision would prevail?

238
11:28.440 --> 11:29.870
Would you accept mine?

239
11:30.390 --> 11:31.200
Well...

240
11:32.320 --> 11:34.480
Would you accept mine?

241
11:35.840 --> 11:36.600
Look.

242
11:42.120 --> 11:43.440
Move faster!

243
11:43.790 --> 11:45.440
Move faster, Liao Chengzhi!

244
11:46.200 --> 11:47.080
Keep moving!

245
11:49.150 --> 11:50.960
Is that Comrade Liao Chengzhi?

246
11:55.720 --> 11:56.550
Wait!

247
12:11.080 --> 12:12.410
Comrade Liao Chengzhi?

248
12:18.030 --> 12:19.360
Don't you remember me?

249
12:20.080 --> 12:21.510
It's Ren Bishi.

250
12:25.120 --> 12:26.000
Comrade Bishi.

251
12:27.030 --> 12:28.360
You two know each other?

252
12:28.720 --> 12:29.480
Yes.

253
12:29.230 --> 12:31.090
[Liao Chengzhi, Former Secretary-General of the Political Department of the 4th Front Army,]

254
12:29.750 --> 12:31.670
He's the son of Mr. Liao Zhongkai.

255
12:31.090 --> 12:32.950
[Son of Liao Zhongkai and He Xiangning]

256
12:31.960 --> 12:33.960
We knew each other back in Shanghai.

257
12:35.550 --> 12:36.480
Comrade Guotao,

258
12:37.840 --> 12:39.840
what did Comrade Chengzhi do wrong?

259
12:41.750 --> 12:43.240
Based on reports from the masses

260
12:43.240 --> 12:45.100
and the evidence we've gathered,

261
12:45.390 --> 12:47.150
Liao Chengzhi infiltrated our ranks

262
12:47.150 --> 12:48.750
to sabotage the revolution.

263
12:48.840 --> 12:50.790
He's a Kuomintang secret agent.

264
12:51.150 --> 12:52.870
Therefore, he's to be expelled from the Party,

265
12:52.870 --> 12:54.930
removed from his post, and detained.

266
12:57.960 --> 12:58.560
Come here.

267
13:01.670 --> 13:02.870
Back in 1932,

268
13:03.480 --> 13:06.670
when Comrade Enlai was overseeing the work in the Soviet areas,

269
13:06.670 --> 13:08.130
he had already recognized

270
13:08.200 --> 13:09.550
the dangers of oversimplifying and expanding the scope

271
13:09.550 --> 13:11.630
of the anti-counterrevolutionary campaign.

272
13:11.630 --> 13:13.000
Why are you still doing this?

273
13:13.000 --> 13:14.120
If this continues,

274
13:14.670 --> 13:16.800
the consequences will be disastrous.

275
13:19.910 --> 13:22.720
When we joined forces with the 3rd Red Army,

276
13:22.840 --> 13:24.200
Comrade He Long told us

277
13:24.270 --> 13:25.360
that Comrade Xia Xi

278
13:25.360 --> 13:26.480
had carried out an anti-counterrevolutionary campaign

279
13:26.480 --> 13:27.840
in the Hunan-Hubei-Xikang Soviet Area.

280
13:27.840 --> 13:29.030
By the time it was over,

281
13:29.030 --> 13:31.630
only 4 Party members in the entire 3rd Red Army

282
13:32.030 --> 13:33.270
were left to take part in Party activities.

283
13:33.270 --> 13:34.870
The rest had to re-register.

284
13:35.550 --> 13:36.510
This approach

285
13:36.840 --> 13:38.770
seriously undermined Party unity

286
13:38.790 --> 13:41.120
and normal political life.

287
13:41.270 --> 13:44.400
It also inflicted tremendous damage on the revolution.

288
13:46.120 --> 13:48.750
But the situation in the 4th Front Army

289
13:48.750 --> 13:53.080
is fundamentally different from that of the 3rd Red Army.

290
13:53.910 --> 13:56.080
Whatever the circumstances, this approach

291
13:56.080 --> 13:57.840
allows personal opinions

292
13:57.840 --> 13:59.720
to take precedence over the Party organization.

293
13:59.720 --> 14:02.980
The officers and soldiers are afraid to speak their minds.

294
14:03.320 --> 14:04.440
How can we expect everyone to unite

295
14:04.440 --> 14:06.640
and overcome the difficulties we face?

296
14:07.630 --> 14:09.390
Among the ranks of our 2nd and 6th Corps,

297
14:09.390 --> 14:11.270
we have Kuomintang lieutenant generals,

298
14:11.270 --> 14:13.510
elderly gentlemen who took part in the 1911 Revolution,

299
14:13.510 --> 14:15.550
and even foreign missionaries

300
14:15.550 --> 14:17.000
who marched alongside us on the Long March.

301
14:17.000 --> 14:18.930
They all came to our aid, after all.

302
14:22.030 --> 14:23.240
As Communists,

303
14:23.270 --> 14:24.600
we must be broad-minded

304
14:27.000 --> 14:29.860
and willing to accept people from all walks of life.

305
14:34.870 --> 14:38.270
To be honest, when I first arrived in the Jiangxi Soviet Area,

306
14:38.440 --> 14:40.600
I once opposed Chairman Mao myself.

307
14:40.600 --> 14:42.960
It didn't take long for me to realize I was wrong.

308
14:42.960 --> 14:44.840
And we certainly shouldn't be so quick

309
14:44.840 --> 14:46.120
to arrest our own comrades.

310
14:46.120 --> 14:47.200
He could have lived comfortably

311
14:47.200 --> 14:49.320
as the son of a prominent Kuomintang elder,

312
14:49.320 --> 14:51.320
but instead, he chose to join us on the Long March.

313
14:51.320 --> 14:53.120
That alone speaks volumes.

314
14:55.720 --> 14:56.750
Comrade Bishi,

315
14:59.200 --> 15:01.910
I understand your good intentions.

316
15:02.150 --> 15:04.390
But the situation in our 4th Front Army

317
15:04.440 --> 15:05.770
is rather complicated.

318
15:06.480 --> 15:08.480
You may not fully understand it yet.

319
15:12.910 --> 15:14.000
Here's what I'll do.

320
15:14.000 --> 15:16.840
I'll look into Liao Chengzhi's case.

321
15:18.320 --> 15:19.240
All right.

322
15:24.870 --> 15:26.080
Comrade Chengzhi,

323
15:27.240 --> 15:28.270
don't worry.

324
15:29.150 --> 15:32.200
Your case will be thoroughly investigated.

325
15:37.000 --> 15:39.670
If you need my help during the investigation,

326
15:39.670 --> 15:40.870
you can come to me.

327
15:43.750 --> 15:44.630
Of course.

328
15:46.850 --> 15:47.690
Of course.

329
16:11.680 --> 16:12.630
Comrade Bishi,

330
16:12.960 --> 16:16.320
I've actually been wanting to hear about all the hardships and dangers

331
16:16.320 --> 16:19.360
your 2nd and 6th Army Corps faced along the way.

332
16:19.870 --> 16:22.240
Since we're both here today,

333
16:22.320 --> 16:23.320
why don't you tell me about it?

334
16:23.320 --> 16:24.590
I'd like to learn from your experience.

335
16:24.590 --> 16:25.350
All right.

336
16:25.960 --> 16:26.750
Please.

337
16:28.840 --> 16:30.790
Liao Chengzhi later recalled

338
16:31.240 --> 16:34.100
that he and Ren Bishi had never actually met before.

339
16:34.120 --> 16:35.840
But not long after this incident,

340
16:35.840 --> 16:37.360
he and several other comrades

341
16:37.360 --> 16:40.320
who had suffered persecution at Zhang Guotao's hands

342
16:40.320 --> 16:42.200
were granted limited freedom.

343
16:42.790 --> 16:43.720
In fact,

344
16:43.720 --> 16:45.790
it was Comrade Bishi who saved them.

345
16:46.000 --> 16:47.550
In the winter of 1936,

346
16:47.550 --> 16:49.790
with Zhou Enlai's intervention,

347
16:49.790 --> 16:51.080
Liao Chengzhi was finally released

348
16:51.080 --> 16:52.870
and reinstated in the Party.

349
16:51.250 --> 16:53.720
[Zhidan County (formerly Bao'an County), Shaanxi]

350
16:55.630 --> 16:56.440
Chairman,

351
16:57.150 --> 16:58.750
the chili peppers are burnt.

352
16:59.750 --> 17:00.910
It's better a little charred. It tastes better that way.

353
17:00.910 --> 17:02.080
More flavorful.

354
17:02.840 --> 17:05.970
Chairman, don't just eat peppers. Have some flatbread.

355
17:13.960 --> 17:14.880
Aren't you eating?

356
17:14.619 --> 17:17.339
[He Qinghua, Mao Zedong's Guard]

357
17:15.069 --> 17:17.880
I... I don't eat much.

358
17:17.960 --> 17:18.750
Nonsense!

359
17:19.640 --> 17:20.369
A growing lad

360
17:20.400 --> 17:21.440
could eat a whole grown man out of house and home.

361
17:21.440 --> 17:22.000
You eat yours.

362
17:22.000 --> 17:22.680
I'll eat mine.

363
17:22.680 --> 17:24.270
No need to worry about each other.

364
17:24.270 --> 17:25.200
Comrade Zedong.

365
17:27.160 --> 17:27.750
Luofu.

366
17:28.069 --> 17:28.720
Enlai.

367
17:29.480 --> 17:31.280
You haven't eaten yet, have you?

368
17:31.510 --> 17:33.400
Perfect. One half for each of you.

369
17:35.270 --> 17:35.960
Qinghua,

370
17:36.480 --> 17:37.310
here, take it.

371
17:37.790 --> 17:38.790
Have you eaten?

372
17:39.110 --> 17:39.920
Yes, I have.

373
17:40.550 --> 17:41.440
Reporting, leaders.

374
17:41.440 --> 17:42.310
The Chairman hasn't eaten.

375
17:42.310 --> 17:43.110
He Qinghua!

376
17:43.920 --> 17:45.720
Don't say another word. Take it.

377
17:45.960 --> 17:47.240
But you really haven't eaten.

378
17:47.240 --> 17:49.570
You're just pretending you're well-fed.

379
17:49.910 --> 17:50.710
Qinghua.

380
17:51.590 --> 17:52.920
I've got an idea for you.

381
17:53.240 --> 17:55.400
Put a notice on the door

382
17:55.400 --> 17:58.240
saying, "Visitors must bring their own food."

383
17:59.440 --> 18:00.830
Did you two bring any food?

384
18:00.830 --> 18:01.510
No.

385
18:01.550 --> 18:03.480
Exactly. We're in a food shortage,

386
18:03.590 --> 18:04.830
and we've run out of food money.

387
18:04.830 --> 18:07.000
So let's all stop pretending we're well-fed.

388
18:07.000 --> 18:07.750
Come on.

389
18:08.070 --> 18:09.160
Let's share it.

390
18:09.390 --> 18:09.990
All right.

391
18:12.200 --> 18:13.590
We didn't bring any food,

392
18:13.590 --> 18:16.640
but we do have some good news for you.

393
18:19.790 --> 18:20.880
The 2nd and 6th Army Corps

394
18:20.880 --> 18:24.000
and the 4th Front Army have split into 3 separate columns.

395
18:24.000 --> 18:28.110
They're heading north from Ganzi, Luhuo, and Suijing.

396
18:28.510 --> 18:29.240
Excellent.

397
18:32.750 --> 18:33.550
This time,

398
18:34.000 --> 18:36.510
Comrades Ren Bishi and He Long

399
18:36.510 --> 18:38.170
have rendered great service.

400
18:38.310 --> 18:41.510
Without the firm support of their two corps for the Central Committee,

401
18:41.510 --> 18:44.440
Zhang Guotao would never have turned back so easily.

402
18:44.680 --> 18:45.790
This clearly shows

403
18:45.790 --> 18:48.790
that our earlier assessment was absolutely correct.

404
18:49.240 --> 18:51.900
We should send a telegram to Peng Dehuai at once,

405
18:52.510 --> 18:54.570
asking him to send the 28th Army south

406
18:54.640 --> 18:57.750
to support the 2nd and 6th Army Corps and the 4th Front Army in their advance north.

407
18:57.750 --> 19:01.160
I also propose merging the 2nd and 6th Army Corps

408
19:01.160 --> 19:05.030
with the 32nd Red Army to form the 2nd Front Army,

409
19:05.440 --> 19:07.590
with He Long as Commander-in-Chief

410
19:07.880 --> 19:09.720
and concurrently Commander of the 2nd Red Army,

411
19:09.720 --> 19:11.780
and Ren Bishi as Political Commissar

412
19:12.440 --> 19:15.240
and concurrently Political Commissar of the 2nd Red Army.

413
19:15.240 --> 19:17.400
This will allow the two Front Armies

414
19:17.400 --> 19:19.920
to coordinate as equals

415
19:19.920 --> 19:21.050
and maintain unity.

416
19:21.320 --> 19:22.050
All right.

417
19:22.080 --> 19:22.720
Agreed.

418
19:23.030 --> 19:25.960
But both Front Armies will have to cross

419
19:27.030 --> 19:28.920
the vast grasslands once again.

420
19:44.310 --> 19:46.720
In early July 1936,

421
19:47.160 --> 19:48.550
the 2nd and 4th Front Armies

422
19:48.550 --> 19:50.680
marched north toward Shaanxi and Gansu in 3 columns,

423
19:50.680 --> 19:53.440
entering the vast grasslands once more.

424
20:01.000 --> 20:01.640
Kid,

425
20:02.110 --> 20:03.270
hang in there.

426
20:05.110 --> 20:06.310
I'll hold on.

427
20:06.920 --> 20:08.310
I'll make it through.

428
20:11.680 --> 20:12.480
How is he?

429
20:14.880 --> 20:16.030
He didn't make it.

430
20:19.750 --> 20:20.640
Listen to me.

431
20:21.030 --> 20:23.000
Even if there's just one breath left in him,

432
20:23.000 --> 20:24.640
you must save him.

433
20:24.640 --> 20:25.550
Understand?

434
20:34.090 --> 20:35.450
[Xiao Ke, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the 2nd Front Army]

435
20:39.080 --> 20:39.800
Come on.

436
20:40.720 --> 20:41.590
Take a look at his leg.

437
20:41.590 --> 20:42.400
All right.

438
20:43.920 --> 20:44.720
Leave it to me.

439
21:03.240 --> 21:04.310
Come on!

440
21:08.590 --> 21:09.830
Are you all right?

441
21:09.880 --> 21:11.480
Give it all you've got. Come on.

442
21:11.480 --> 21:15.440
Come on! One, two, three!

443
21:17.080 --> 21:17.710
Come on.

444
21:18.160 --> 21:18.680
Division Commander Lu.

445
21:18.680 --> 21:20.000
Come on. One!

446
21:19.990 --> 21:20.790
Division Commander Lu.

447
21:20.790 --> 21:21.640
Up!

448
21:22.550 --> 21:23.830
Put me down.

449
21:25.450 --> 21:26.780
Division Commander Lu.

450
21:28.270 --> 21:29.070
You're here.

451
21:29.150 --> 21:30.260
[Zhang Zhenhan, Tactics Instructor at the Red Army School,]

452
21:30.260 --> 21:31.370
[Former Lieutenant General and Commander of the Kuomintang's 42nd Division]

453
21:32.070 --> 21:33.130
Instructor Zhang.

454
21:33.830 --> 21:35.400
What is it, Instructor Zhang?

455
21:35.400 --> 21:36.330
Leave the cannon

456
21:37.240 --> 21:38.030
behind.

457
21:37.640 --> 21:41.320
[Lu Dongsheng, Commander of the 4th Division, 2nd Red Army]

458
21:39.550 --> 21:42.030
Have you lost your mind?

459
21:42.440 --> 21:45.000
How can you teach without the cannon?

460
21:53.350 --> 21:54.310
Comrade Zhou.

461
21:57.240 --> 22:00.110
Niu. Niu!

462
22:01.640 --> 22:03.680
Doctor! Doctor!

463
22:03.720 --> 22:05.830
Hurry! Doctor!

464
22:06.070 --> 22:09.160
See what's wrong with Niu. Niu.

465
22:11.880 --> 22:13.030
Comrade Zhou.

466
22:14.000 --> 22:15.710
[Zhou Suyuan, Commander of the Guizhou Anti-Japanese National Salvation Army]

467
22:16.550 --> 22:18.920
Niu!

468
22:19.150 --> 22:20.590
Niu.

469
22:21.720 --> 22:24.640
It's all my fault!

470
22:25.370 --> 22:27.330
Niu!

471
22:27.830 --> 22:31.200
Wake up, Niu! Niu!

472
22:31.370 --> 22:32.810
Niu!

473
22:32.840 --> 22:34.050
Comrade Zhou.

474
22:34.680 --> 22:35.160
Come on.

475
22:38.510 --> 22:39.510
Commander,

476
22:40.160 --> 22:43.400
I'm old and no longer any use.

477
22:44.270 --> 22:46.200
I beg you,

478
22:46.880 --> 22:49.640
leave an old man like me here.

479
22:49.920 --> 22:52.160
I can't keep holding up the troops

480
22:52.590 --> 22:55.070
and burdening my comrades.

481
22:55.360 --> 22:56.790
Comrade Zhou,

482
22:58.480 --> 23:00.000
you must hold on.

483
23:00.030 --> 23:01.920
You must make it out of these grasslands.

484
23:01.920 --> 23:04.270
We must reach northern Shaanxi together.

485
23:04.440 --> 23:05.500
That's the only way

486
23:05.830 --> 23:08.640
to honor all the care Niu has given you.

487
23:11.590 --> 23:13.790
Niu!

488
23:33.000 --> 23:34.680
Take good care of Comrade Zhou.

489
23:34.680 --> 23:35.310
Yes,

490
23:35.140 --> 23:35.900
Commander.

491
23:37.170 --> 23:38.260
Comrade Zhou,

492
23:39.110 --> 23:40.270
let me carry you.

493
23:54.400 --> 23:56.310
In October 1936,

494
23:56.550 --> 23:58.720
Zhou Suyuan completed the Long March

495
23:58.720 --> 24:00.590
with the 2nd Front Army.

496
24:00.960 --> 24:02.480
After the founding of the PRC,

497
24:02.480 --> 24:05.880
he served successively as a member of the Southwest Military and Political Committee,

498
24:05.880 --> 24:08.480
Vice Chairman of the Guizhou Provincial People's Government,

499
24:08.480 --> 24:10.240
a member of the National Committee of the CPPCC,

500
24:10.240 --> 24:12.550
and Vice Governor of Guizhou Province.

501
24:13.030 --> 24:14.880
As we crossed the snow-capped mountains,

502
24:14.880 --> 24:16.000
two comrades

503
24:16.790 --> 24:18.400
have already died saving me.

504
24:18.680 --> 24:20.410
We can't let this happen again.

505
24:20.750 --> 24:21.880
We can't abandon it.

506
24:22.160 --> 24:24.880
I made a solemn promise to the Commander.

507
24:25.160 --> 24:26.790
Neither you nor the cannon can be left behind.

508
24:26.790 --> 24:28.790
Both of you must be taken out of here.

509
24:29.790 --> 24:31.270
Who are you people?

510
24:31.750 --> 24:33.200
Get up! Are you all right?

511
24:36.550 --> 24:37.750
What did you just say?

512
24:39.070 --> 24:40.270
Instructor Zhang asked

513
24:40.270 --> 24:42.000
what kind of people we all were.

514
24:45.640 --> 24:46.240
Well,

515
24:46.440 --> 24:49.030
I was born into a tenant farmer's family.

516
24:49.480 --> 24:51.350
I used to herd cattle for a landlord.

517
24:51.350 --> 24:53.750
Then I worked as an apprentice in a factory.

518
24:54.200 --> 24:57.440
Later, I joined the revolution with the second young master

519
24:57.440 --> 24:58.370
of our household

520
24:58.590 --> 25:00.250
and became a Red Army soldier.

521
25:00.310 --> 25:01.710
That's all there is to it.

522
25:02.240 --> 25:03.640
The second young master?

523
25:05.480 --> 25:07.590
Chen Geng is my second young master.

524
25:08.160 --> 25:10.350
The very same Chen Geng who saved Chiang Kai-shek?

525
25:10.350 --> 25:13.550
That's his biggest regret.

526
25:14.000 --> 25:15.550
He's told me countless times

527
25:15.550 --> 25:19.210
how he wished he'd dropped Chiang Kai-shek to his death back then.

528
25:19.920 --> 25:22.980
If he'd dropped Chiang Kai-shek to his death back then,

529
25:23.440 --> 25:25.770
you wouldn't have had to suffer like this.

530
25:26.830 --> 25:27.890
Come on, comrades!

531
25:27.920 --> 25:29.960
Let's put our backs into it and get this cannon out!

532
25:29.960 --> 25:30.960
Come on! Let's go!

533
25:31.880 --> 25:32.640
Be careful!

534
25:33.070 --> 25:34.550
Wait for my command. Ready!

535
25:34.550 --> 25:37.030
One, two, lift!

536
25:40.350 --> 25:41.160
Get up.

537
25:41.920 --> 25:46.160
Again! One, two, lift!

538
25:46.160 --> 25:48.160
This cannon, serial number 587,

539
25:48.160 --> 25:50.750
weighing 386 kilograms,

540
25:50.750 --> 25:53.720
is a 75mm mountain gun modeled after the Krupp design.

541
25:53.720 --> 25:55.240
It was the only mountain gun

542
25:55.240 --> 25:58.000
the Red Army brought all the way to northern Shaanxi during the Long March.

543
25:58.000 --> 26:01.440
It later served with the 120th Division of the Eighth Route Army,

544
26:01.440 --> 26:04.830
where it proved its worth in the War of Resistance Against Japan.

545
26:04.830 --> 26:06.110
It is now housed at

546
26:06.110 --> 26:09.310
the Military Museum of the Chinese People's Revolution.

547
26:12.200 --> 26:13.640
After arriving in northern Shaanxi

548
26:13.640 --> 26:16.550
in October 1936, Zhang Zhenhan

549
26:16.640 --> 26:20.640
continued to serve as Chief Tactical Instructor at the Red Army School.

550
26:20.710 --> 26:22.310
After the founding of the PRC,

551
26:22.310 --> 26:25.200
he served as Vice Mayor of Changsha,

552
26:25.680 --> 26:27.880
a Standing Committee member of the Hunan Provincial Committee of the CPPCC,

553
26:27.880 --> 26:31.480
and a member of the National Committee of the CPPCC, among other positions.

554
26:31.480 --> 26:33.160
Watch out. Come on.

555
26:35.800 --> 26:36.360
Come on.

556
26:44.790 --> 26:45.480
Careful.

557
26:45.950 --> 26:46.520
Careful.

558
26:54.110 --> 26:55.070
Watch your step.

559
27:00.870 --> 27:01.390
Come on.

560
27:27.560 --> 27:28.360
Careful.

561
27:45.880 --> 27:46.880
Hang in there.

562
27:56.880 --> 27:59.030
Hang in there.

563
28:02.330 --> 28:03.120
Come on.

564
28:07.070 --> 28:08.330
Commander-in-Chief.

565
28:15.270 --> 28:16.350
Comrade Guotao.

566
28:20.110 --> 28:21.110
How much farther?

567
28:21.640 --> 28:24.830
According to the scouts up ahead,

568
28:25.440 --> 28:27.840
we haven't even covered half the distance.

569
28:29.880 --> 28:31.010
Still that far to go?

570
28:32.790 --> 28:33.720
Comrade Guotao,

571
28:35.270 --> 28:37.590
this is our first time crossing the grasslands,

572
28:37.590 --> 28:38.720
but many of them

573
28:39.550 --> 28:41.590
are making their third crossing.

574
28:45.720 --> 28:47.720
We've suffered far too many losses.

575
28:48.920 --> 28:49.850
Comrade Guotao,

576
28:50.640 --> 28:53.400
if the Songpan Campaign

577
28:53.400 --> 28:55.110
had gone ahead as planned,

578
28:55.440 --> 28:58.960
many of them wouldn't have perished here.

579
29:14.040 --> 29:14.600
Come on.

580
29:15.830 --> 29:18.550
Watch your step.

581
29:19.750 --> 29:20.440
You.

582
29:21.350 --> 29:22.200
Take my horse.

583
29:24.350 --> 29:25.000
Chief Political Commissar,

584
29:25.000 --> 29:25.960
I can't ride.

585
29:25.960 --> 29:27.310
That's an order!

586
29:28.090 --> 29:28.980
Yes, sir.

587
29:45.070 --> 29:45.800
Give it to me.

588
29:46.350 --> 29:47.310
Hand it over!

589
30:28.590 --> 30:29.310
Come on.

590
30:29.580 --> 30:30.310
Come on.

591
30:32.270 --> 30:34.440
Hang in there!

592
31:21.370 --> 31:25.070
[Zhang Side, Soldier of the 4th Front Army]

593
31:24.350 --> 31:28.400
That's where the squad leader lost his life.

594
31:57.030 --> 31:57.830
Squad Leader.

595
31:59.030 --> 32:00.490
This is my third time here.

596
32:01.830 --> 32:04.090
And I've brought Ximei here with me, too.

597
32:07.200 --> 32:09.600
I truly don't want there to be a fourth time.

598
32:33.590 --> 32:34.550
Ximei.

599
34:23.770 --> 34:24.810
Ximei.

600
34:34.730 --> 34:44.040
♪ Barefoot wading through the stream ♪

601
34:44.070 --> 34:54.130
♪ Fish swish their tails in wooden tubs ♪

602
34:54.880 --> 35:04.750
♪ A hawk carries clouds of color away ♪

603
35:05.320 --> 35:17.550
♪ My dog chases through three ravines ♪

604
35:20.960 --> 35:21.670
Come on.

605
36:16.960 --> 36:20.800
Yu! Yu! Yu!

606
36:21.000 --> 36:21.880
Yu!

607
36:28.110 --> 36:29.020
Yu!

608
36:33.760 --> 36:35.440
Yu. Yu.

609
36:36.880 --> 36:38.130
Yu!

610
36:46.480 --> 36:47.630
How's your wound?

611
36:49.550 --> 36:50.880
It's starting to stink.

612
36:51.030 --> 36:52.920
I'm afraid the arm can't be saved.

613
36:52.390 --> 36:55.680
[He Bingyan, Commander of the 6th Division, 2nd Red Army]

614
36:53.440 --> 36:54.550
Director He said

615
36:54.880 --> 36:56.150
we'd find a chance to amputate it

616
36:56.080 --> 36:58.940
[Yu Qiuli, Former Political Commissar of the 18th Regiment, 6th Division, 2nd Red Army]

617
36:56.670 --> 36:58.670
once we're through the grasslands.

618
37:01.110 --> 37:04.110
He knows his stuff.

619
37:08.320 --> 37:09.110
Yu,

620
37:09.920 --> 37:11.280
you know,

621
37:12.000 --> 37:14.000
we both came from the 18th Regiment.

622
37:14.070 --> 37:16.270
One of us was the regimental commander,

623
37:16.400 --> 37:18.000
the other the political commissar.

624
37:18.000 --> 37:19.360
I've lost my right arm.

625
37:19.710 --> 37:21.480
If you have your left arm amputated too,

626
37:21.480 --> 37:22.680
word will get around,

627
37:22.920 --> 37:24.670
and everyone in the country

628
37:24.670 --> 37:27.440
will think our 18th Regiment is cursed.

629
37:31.880 --> 37:32.670
We

630
37:33.320 --> 37:34.760
Communists

631
37:36.030 --> 37:37.690
don't believe in such things.

632
37:39.160 --> 37:39.910
Come on.

633
38:04.840 --> 38:05.900
I'll help you walk.

634
38:09.280 --> 38:10.070
See?

635
38:11.070 --> 38:12.320
That's more like it.

636
38:12.550 --> 38:14.480
We help each other out.

637
38:16.710 --> 38:19.770
Put us together, and we've still got a good pair of arms.

638
38:23.110 --> 38:24.510
Two months later,

639
38:24.800 --> 38:27.550
as Yu Qiuli's injury continued to deteriorate,

640
38:27.550 --> 38:29.350
his left arm had to be amputated.

641
38:29.800 --> 38:32.030
After the nationwide resistance against Japan began,

642
38:32.030 --> 38:35.070
He Bingyan and Yu Qiuli teamed up once again.

643
38:35.230 --> 38:37.440
They served respectively as Commander

644
38:37.440 --> 38:39.800
and Political Commissar of the 120th Division's

645
38:39.800 --> 38:41.480
Independent 3rd Detachment of the Eighth Route Army.

646
38:41.480 --> 38:43.440
The people called this unit

647
38:43.440 --> 38:44.700
the "One-Armed Unit."

648
38:44.920 --> 38:46.960
After several subsequent reorganizations,

649
38:46.960 --> 38:48.280
it eventually became

650
38:48.280 --> 38:49.840
the 1st Regiment of the 1st Division,

651
38:49.840 --> 38:53.550
1st Army of the Chinese PLA.

652
38:54.980 --> 38:57.980
[Zhidan County (formerly Bao'an County), Shaanxi]

653
39:09.320 --> 39:10.880
How is it, Luofu?

654
39:12.190 --> 39:14.920
We haven't received any telegrams yet.

655
39:15.400 --> 39:17.440
It seems the 2nd and 4th Front Armies

656
39:17.840 --> 39:19.840
must be facing tremendous difficulties.

657
39:19.840 --> 39:22.800
I don't think we need to be too pessimistic.

658
39:23.480 --> 39:25.340
The comrades in both Front Armies

659
39:25.510 --> 39:27.480
have weathered many trials.

660
39:27.840 --> 39:30.030
I'm sure they'll overcome every obstacle

661
39:30.030 --> 39:31.070
and reach southern Gansu

662
39:31.070 --> 39:33.840
by early August as originally planned.

663
39:34.230 --> 39:35.880
We must have faith in them.

664
39:38.960 --> 39:40.440
Jiaxiang makes a good point.

665
39:40.440 --> 39:40.760
All right.

666
39:40.760 --> 39:43.670
I don't think we should just sit around waiting.

667
39:43.670 --> 39:46.000
We need to make the necessary preparations

668
39:46.000 --> 39:47.760
for the upcoming reunion of all 3 main forces.

669
39:47.760 --> 39:48.630
First,

670
39:48.630 --> 39:50.800
the second phase of the Western Front Army's

671
39:50.800 --> 39:52.920
Westward Expedition has been completed.

672
39:52.920 --> 39:55.550
We can telegraph Peng Dehuai to have his troops rest and regroup where they are

673
39:55.550 --> 39:57.010
and prepare to march south

674
39:57.070 --> 40:00.270
to meet the 2nd and 4th Front Armies as they advance north.

675
40:01.760 --> 40:02.590
Second,

676
40:02.880 --> 40:06.190
to strengthen the leadership of the 2nd and 4th Front Armies

677
40:06.190 --> 40:07.880
and prevent the problems we faced before,

678
40:07.880 --> 40:08.920
I propose

679
40:09.280 --> 40:10.960
that the Central Committee approve the establishment of

680
40:10.960 --> 40:12.400
the Northwest Bureau of the CPC Central Committee.

681
40:12.400 --> 40:13.600
The Northwest Bureau

682
40:13.920 --> 40:14.920
will take unified command

683
40:14.920 --> 40:17.520
of the 2nd and 4th Front Armies' advance north.

684
40:18.070 --> 40:18.880
Agreed.

685
40:19.190 --> 40:19.980
Agreed.

686
40:20.010 --> 40:20.700
Agreed.

687
40:23.670 --> 40:26.550
On July 27, 1936,

688
40:26.710 --> 40:28.670
the Central Military Commission issued an order

689
40:28.670 --> 40:30.670
to end the Westward Expedition.

690
40:31.510 --> 40:33.920
The expedition lasted more than 2 months.

691
40:33.920 --> 40:36.960
In total, the Red Army annihilated 7 Kuomintang battalions,

692
40:36.960 --> 40:39.510
routed 3 regiments and another 5 battalions,

693
40:39.760 --> 40:41.800
captured over 2,000 enemy soldiers,

694
40:41.800 --> 40:44.000
and occupied more than 10 towns.

695
40:44.070 --> 40:47.590
It established a new base area stretching over 200 kilometers in both directions,

696
40:47.590 --> 40:49.760
creating favorable conditions for the junction

697
40:49.760 --> 40:51.710
of the 3 main Red Army forces.

698
40:52.110 --> 40:52.970
On the same day,

699
40:53.070 --> 40:56.590
the Central Committee approved the establishment of the Northwest Bureau of the CPC Central Committee,

700
40:56.590 --> 40:58.510
with Zhang Guotao as Secretary

701
40:58.510 --> 41:00.590
and Ren Bishi as Deputy Secretary.

702
41:00.800 --> 41:04.550
Zhu De, Guan Xiangying, He Long, Xu Xiangqian,

703
41:04.550 --> 41:07.920
Wang Zhen, Chen Changhao, and others were appointed as members.

704
41:07.920 --> 41:08.760
The Bureau would exercise unified command

705
41:08.760 --> 41:11.550
over the 2nd and 4th Front Armies' advance north.

706
41:30.770 --> 41:31.290
Here.

707
41:32.280 --> 41:33.410
Take some firewood.

708
41:40.030 --> 41:40.640
Here.

709
41:41.440 --> 41:42.500
Add some more wood.

710
41:47.670 --> 41:48.670
Hang in there, Li!

711
41:49.320 --> 41:51.230
Li! Li!

712
41:51.400 --> 41:52.190
Li!

713
41:52.520 --> 41:53.020
Li!

714
41:53.150 --> 41:54.150
What's wrong?

715
41:54.150 --> 41:55.680
He just ate some wild herbs.

716
41:55.920 --> 41:56.710
Which herbs?

717
41:56.880 --> 41:57.510
These.

718
41:59.630 --> 42:01.070
These are fleabane weeds.

719
42:01.070 --> 42:02.760
Our comrades who taste-test wild plants warned us

720
42:02.760 --> 42:03.440
that they're irritating

721
42:03.440 --> 42:05.900
and shouldn't be eaten in large quantities.

722
42:06.920 --> 42:07.670
Huang,

723
42:08.230 --> 42:10.030
do you have anything else to eat?

724
42:15.590 --> 42:16.400
This is water celery.

725
42:16.400 --> 42:17.330
It's safe to eat.

726
42:21.880 --> 42:22.800
Comrades,

727
42:23.360 --> 42:26.070
we've organized plant-tasting activities in every company

728
42:26.070 --> 42:28.000
to help you learn to tell

729
42:28.000 --> 42:29.070
which wild plants are safe to eat

730
42:29.070 --> 42:30.730
and which ones are poisonous.

731
42:30.760 --> 42:32.190
For example, water celery,

732
42:32.190 --> 42:34.670
plantain, and lamb's quarters are all edible.

733
42:34.670 --> 42:36.130
But fleabane like this...

734
42:36.440 --> 42:37.000
Right.

735
42:37.670 --> 42:39.270
And there's more. Look here.

736
42:40.030 --> 42:41.090
Plants like these,

737
42:41.320 --> 42:43.360
aconite, wolf's bane,

738
42:44.000 --> 42:45.550
and lousewort

739
42:45.550 --> 42:47.150
are all poisonous. Remember that.

740
42:47.150 --> 42:47.750
All right.

741
42:50.070 --> 42:51.760
Hang in there. Don't fall asleep.

742
42:51.760 --> 42:52.840
Don't fall asleep!

743
42:54.320 --> 42:56.760
Hongxia! Hongxia, wake up!

744
42:57.400 --> 42:58.190
Hongxia!

745
42:58.840 --> 43:00.440
Hongxia, don't fall asleep!

746
43:00.800 --> 43:01.920
Hongxia, wake up!

747
43:02.170 --> 43:03.420
Hang in there!
